OpenTelemetry:
What is observability:
To define the application is stable, stability defined from application NFR's like availability, reliability and performance. If the application is stable the user is not facing any issues. How do we know if the application is stable, that usually define from state of the system, how do we know the state ie using output mesurement of the system. The process of using iutput mesurement and define the state of the system is called observability.What output mesurement we see is metrics, logs and traces.With this output mesurement we define the stability of system if any issue we fix the application based on output mesurements. These metrics, logs and traces we called as telemetrt signals

Telemetry signals:
Metrics: Numeric msururemets collected over time. Single mesurement collected at a moment eg cpu of LG at 5:34 PM or acumalated data ie number req/sec.
Logs - Actual logs of the system
Teaces - Request path with trace id to other microservices with its response time will shown in trace

Monitoring Vs Observability:
Monitoring:
It will check the health of the system and raise the incidednt based on static threshold we set and wont provide what cause this issue. Monitoring happen through metrics and logs.
Observability: It to the same but it give what cause the issue based on trace data and have dynamic threshold for incident based on AI and ML model. It monitor metrics, logs and traces.

Reliability Metrics:
MTTD - Mean time to detect. When issue happen how much time we took to detect
MTTR - Mean time to Resolve. After the issue is detected how much time we took to resolve.
MTBR - Mean time between failure. After we fix the issue how much time application was stable until the next failure happen.Time between MTTR to Failure is MTBR
MTTF- Mean time to Failure. The total time from first failure to second failure. 
If we have observability in picture, MTTR will be quick so MTBR woont happen and MTTR also will be less.Because of tracing feature we will fix it permenantly and quickly

Observability Solutions:
We have 3 component
Software system - Where we collect the telemetry data using agent, api/sdk ie writing code on application code
Transmitting data - Here the collected data will be transmitted to backend service via http or other protocal. It use two ways direct and proxy. If proxy it will process, aggregate and compress the collected data and send to backend.
Backend - Where we will process and analyse the data.
Opentelemetry will come into the picture of first two system, backed we can choose which we want to use to process and analyse the data.

OpenTelemetry Collector:
It an OpenTelemetry component and act as intermediate between application datasource and backend which will collect , process and export to backend.


OpenTelemetry:
Its an opensource, it generate, collect and export the telemetry data.
What data it generate and collect:
It generate and collect logs, traces and metrics and how it will do is through zero code, library and code based which called as instrumentation.Api and sdk will come come into picture of zero code and code based.
How data is exported to backend:
The generated and collected data are received , proceessed and exported to backend using the OTLP ie opentelemetry proctcol with collector ie proxy to backend services. OTLP is opentelemetry protocal to transmit the data to backend and we have other protacol to transmit the data to backend apart from OTLP which is developed by other source to export the instrume nted data.

Instrumentation:
3 Instrumentation
Zero Code - Install agent it will collect all data
Code based - Write custom code on application code to collect data
Library - External libarary to collect data, need manual intervention

Zero Code agent - Installing the agent , it will collect all the http and database connections ie inbound and outbound connections to the applications but not the custom code logic. Only with limited language support and wont collect all database data
eBPF - Also an agent installed at kernal level, only support linux and capture more detailed metric but for custom code it wont capture. Support more language, protacol and databases

